	<p>When transporting your two-wheeler vehicle from Saharsa, it is crucial to have the following essential paperwork ready:</p>

	<p>The Vehicle Registration Certificate (RC) is a vital document that verifies the ownership and details of your bike. Make sure to obtain a self-attested copy of the RC, which means someone other than the owner signs the copy as proof of its authenticity.</p>

	<p>Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate confirms that your bike meets the necessary emission standards and is roadworthy. Ensure that you possess a valid PUC issued within the last six months before the transportation begins.</p>

	<p>Insurance is mandatory for all vehicles in India to protect both you and others in case of accidents or damages. Ensure that your bike's insurance is valid and up to date before transportation.</p>

	<p>In case of bike transportation through any authorized service provider, it is mandatory to have an IBA-approved (Indian Bike Association) consignment bill of entry. This document serves as evidence of the consignment and its details, ensuring a smooth transportation process.</p>

	<p>To protect your interests in case of any loss or damage during transportation, you must declare the full market value of your bike. Prepare a signed declaration indicating the declared value, which will be used to settle any potential claims.</p>

