      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Saharsa</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Upon the arrival of your two-wheeler or motorcycle at the designated destination, the delivery process transitions to a critical verification phase designed to ensure transparency and mutual agreement on the vehicle's status. This handover protocol is strictly enforced under daylight conditions to eliminate visual ambiguities caused by artificial lighting or shadows.</p>
<p>The recipient must conduct a thorough re-inspection of the vehicle, directly comparing its current physical state against the high-resolution pickup photos documented at the origin. This step-by-step visual audit is essential to confirm that no new scratches, dents, or mechanical anomalies have occurred during transit.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Daylight Visual Inspection:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The recipient must examine the vehicle under natural daylight. Compare every body panel, wheel, and component against the original pickup photographs. Any discrepancy, such as new paint chips or bent mirrors, must be noted immediately and reported to the delivery executive before accepting the keys.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Odometer Verification:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Cross-reference the current odometer reading on the dashboard with the figure recorded on the Legal Receipt (LR) bilty. The difference should only account for the distance traveled during logistics. A significant variance may indicate tampering or unauthorized usage, which must be flagged instantly.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Functional Quick Check:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Briefly test essential functions including lights, indicators, horn, and brake responsiveness to ensure the vehicle is mechanically sound and ready for immediate use upon handover.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Signed Condition Sign-Off:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Once the inspection is satisfactory and all details match the documentation, the recipient must sign the condition sign-off form. This legal document certifies that the vehicle was delivered in the agreed-upon condition. Retain a copy of this signed document along with the LR bilty for future reference or insurance claims.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p>This rigorous procedure protects both the customer and the logistics provider. By meticulously verifying the odometer against the LR bilty and confirming the physical condition against pickup images, you establish a clear baseline of accountability.</p>
<p>Do not hesitate to pause the handover if any doubt remains. Ensuring that the signed condition sign-off is completed only after full verification guarantees that your investment is protected from the moment you take possession of the keys.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



